  "verdict": "SATURATED IN EVERY FAMILY \u2014 all 8 linear families tested drive a pair that should be inseparable to AUROC >= 0.95 (worst case 1.000). Held-out AUROC on a fitted contrast is uninformative in this regime regardless of estimator, so the standing 'diff-of-means only' caveat is answered: saturation is a property of n ~ 25-50 per side in d = 3584, not of the direction-finding method. The most conservative family tested was diff_of_means at 1.000. The floor says how little of this is direction-finding: a RANDOM direction, signed on fit rows and never fitted, averages AUROC 0.738 at a fixed layer and 0.941 once it is also allowed to pick its layer from the same 29. Layer selection alone is therefore worth +0.203 AUROC to a direction carrying no information, which is a second vacuous criterion sitting inside the first. The disconfirming test named in results/affordance.md also fails for every family: fitted the way an auditor would fit it, each of the 8 reads concealed and disclosed steering identically, largest gap +0.000. The affordance inversion's standing caveat \u2014 that it was measured for diff-of-means only and a regularised or non-mean-based probe might have separated them \u2014 is answered for the linear families tested."
